       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>The SPARQL results format doesn't actually support nesting for TQL queries at all.  Probably this ticket should be renamed to add support for the TQL results format - without that the power of TQL subqueries is somewhat lost.</p>\n\n<p>(and should be noted that in Mulgara 2.1.4 there's an error in the TQL results output with subqueries - invalid XML is produced, so will need a Mulgara upgrade also)</p>",
     "created": "06/Dec/11 4:46 PM",
     "id": "12142",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10980/comment/12142",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
